id: SCA-034
title: Suspicious npm unscoped package with private naming pattern
category: supply-chain
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: package.json
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: "name"\s*:\s*"(private|corp|company|internal)-
    message: Unscoped package with private naming pattern — vulnerable to dependency confusion. An attacker publishes a higher version on public npm, and npm installs it.
fix: Always use scoped packages (@yourorg/package-name) for private packages. Configure .npmrc with @yourorg:registry=https://your-private-registry.
